Notebook[{
Cell["ExtendInfraSegment", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"a2ce585e-247a-4ed3-b076-1d11cd24fcc5"],

Cell["[LLM Generated]", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"03e74c5f-0a38-4928-bfd3-894a8f309a8a"],

Cell["\<\
ExtendInfraSegment[graph, a, b, c, d] returns InfraPoint[{x}] for x with B(a, \
b, x) and d(b, x) == d(c, d) (Tarski axiom A4 synthetic-extension). \
ExtendInfraSegment[graph, a, b, c, d, n] / UpTo[n] / All controls \
multiplicity. The 2-arg ExtendInfraSegment[graph, segment] form (extend \
segment to a maximal line) has been removed; use FindInfraLine[graph, \
segment] for the geodesic case or ExtendInfraPath[graph, segment, All, \
Properties -> {\"Simple\", {\"ShortestPath\"}}] for per-step extension.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a75a188f-2f5d-4868-8607-6f1d1a1dbb9c"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"26fe41b4-5415-46d9-8c1b-695e3b91af58"],

Cell["Load the paclet.", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"77d30578-b4af-4191-92ea-14a1954d957c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<WolframInstitute`SyntheticInfrageometry`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Code",
 InitializationCell->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"4660ebd5-718e-4b49-a202-44f8512ea408"],

Cell["Related Guides", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ba79cf6d-6215-4aee-a34f-4c234a1780a0"],

Cell["EuclideanGeometryGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1bd2fffd-e337-4fbe-84dc-f52fc57080b1"],

Cell["SyntheticInfrageometryGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2f0d0b75-8cc1-472b-bff6-56a7629ba62e"]
},
